      'You can place the common law’s own story beside it — land transferred to a trusted holder by men leaving on crusade, holders who refused to give it back, a court that enforced the arrangement in conscience, a king who struck at it in 1535 because it cost him his fees, and lawyers who found the holes within a generation.',
      'You hold the sentence that keeps a modern family humble about all of it: "there is no new thing under the sun" (Ecclesiastes 1:9). Knowing the fight is how you use the tool instead of being used by it.',
